            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LaDonna Langwell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It really doesn't get any easier then this. Like others, we softened them in oil first, then made the red sauce and dipped the softened tortillas in the sauce before filling. We used a leftover taco beef because we had it and chose to add the onions raw to the inside rather then cook them. Either way, this is an easy and delicious recipe!",
